.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3504x1971+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3504x1971+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3504x1971+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3504x1971+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3504x1971+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3504x1971+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3504x1971+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa4%2F9a%2Fc3ba63214478a3e7622cf259d6f6%2F4d191f7a-3395-434e-a9b6-a9df6e767048.jpg" class="img" alt="Florence Pugh in East of Eden." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Florence Pugh in East of Eden.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Geoffrey Short/Netflix                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check out what &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/culture/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is watching, reading and listening to this weekend:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍿 Movies:&lt;/strong&gt; Oscar-winning documentarian Alex Gibney spent four years researching tech billionaire Elon Musk by reviewing extensive documents and interviewing people close to him. The nearly four-hour film, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/07/nx-s1-5960380/musk-film-alex-gibney" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Musk&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;,&lt;/em&gt; is in theaters today ahead of its HBO release.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📺 TV:&lt;/strong&gt; Netflix's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/07/nx-s1-5992662/east-of-eden-brings-a-light-modern-touch-to-an-epic-literary-classic" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;East of Eden&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, starring Florence Pugh, offers an epic retelling of an American classic that provides a fresh perspective, &lt;em&gt;Pop Culture Happy Hour&lt;/em&gt; says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📚 Books:&lt;/strong&gt; It's time to say goodbye to beach reads and welcome cozy autumn books. NPR's &lt;em&gt;Book of the Day&lt;/em&gt; host Andrew Limbong shares &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/02/nx-s1-5983820/what-to-read-books-fiction-nonfiction" target="_blank"&gt;10 exciting books&lt;/a&gt; coming this fall, featuring titles from Barbara Kingsolver, Chad Harbach, Jasmine Guillory and more.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎵 Music:&lt;/strong&gt; Troye Sivan's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/07/nx-s1-5887547/troye-sivan-shes-the-best-interview" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;She's The Best&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; explores darker feelings with a mix of gloom and bright, bombastic moments, all while continuing to honor the legacy of queer dance floors in his music videos, NPR Music's Isabella Gomez Sarmiento says.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎭 Theater:&lt;/strong&gt; In the Broadway play &lt;em&gt;School Girls; or, the African Mean Girls Play&lt;/em&gt;, the ladies at Aburi Girls' Boarding School navigate difficult lessons through their friendships, conflicts and the upcoming Miss Ghana 1986 beauty pageant. Playwright Jocelyn Bioh and director Whitney White join &lt;em&gt;It's Been A Minute&lt;/em&gt; host Brittany Luse to &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5993461:x" target="_blank"&gt;discuss the story's significance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;❓ Quiz: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/10/09/g-s1-147111/trump-bts-paramount-tv-el-nino-news-quiz" target="_blank"&gt;This week's quiz&lt;/a&gt; will test your knowledge on protests, Nobels and even a K-pop superstar. While I may not have a prize for you upon completion, I can provide a hint: at least two of the answers were featured in the "Today's top stories" section of &lt;em&gt;this &lt;/em&gt;newsletter this week.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147440" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4500;         --source-height: 2531;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Fa5%2F406685634c73a582ad680acd20db%2Fgettyimages-2220014397.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Fa5%2F406685634c73a582ad680acd20db%2Fgettyimages-2220014397.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Fa5%2F406685634c73a582ad680acd20db%2Fgettyimages-2220014397.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Fa5%2F406685634c73a582ad680acd20db%2Fgettyimages-2220014397.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Fa5%2F406685634c73a582ad680acd20db%2Fgettyimages-2220014397.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Fa5%2F406685634c73a582ad680acd20db%2Fgettyimages-2220014397.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4500x2531+0+234/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Fa5%2F406685634c73a5