tcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1920x1080+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fad%2Fa2%2F998e88bf412283021f9ebee697be%2Fpostcard-lahore.jpg" class="img" alt="postcard-lahore.jpg" loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;NPR's Diaa Hadid is sending greetings from &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/07/nx-s1-5992681/lahore-pakistan-high-court-square" target="_blank"&gt;the Lahore High Court&lt;/a&gt; in Pakistan for this week's installment of Far-Flung Postcards. She describes it as "a near-perfect example of British South Asian colonial architecture."&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Opal Lee, the Grandmother of Juneteenth, &lt;a href="https://www.kera.org/2026/10/07/civil-rights-icon-opal-lee-celebrates-100th-birthday-by-clearing-the-way-for-new-museum/" target="_blank"&gt;celebrated her 100th birthday&lt;/a&gt; at the future site of the National Juneteenth Museum in Texas. (via &lt;a href="https://www.kera.org/" target="_blank"&gt;KERA&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A remarkably intact fossil discovery has given scientists new evidence about when the &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/07/nx-s1-5991361/fossil-mammal-platypus-chew-swallow-suckle-earliest" target="_blank"&gt;ability to chew and swallow food&lt;/a&gt; emerged among mammals.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
