      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Cornell University sexual assault case that produced no criminal charges is now under state scrutiny.&lt;/strong&gt; New York Gov. Kathy Hochul appointed &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/01/nx-s1-5987703/cornell-fraternity-rape-case-updates" target="_blank"&gt;Attorney General Letitia James' office as special prosecutor&lt;/a&gt; after new information raised questions about what campus police shared with the local district attorney. NPR confirmed the woman who reported the assault gave police a detailed account, including that she had been raped.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-145930" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 6000;         --source-height: 3375;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6000x3375+0+313/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F04%2Fae%2F1025ebf4402dbf76ac6913d50406%2Fgettyimages-2297899878.jpg" class="img" alt="Students walk on the campus of Cornell University on Wednesday in Ithaca, N.Y." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Students walk on the campus of Cornell University on Wednesday in Ithaca, N.Y.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Spencer Platt/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;NPR's Brian Mann tells &lt;em&gt;Up First&lt;/em&gt; the case has &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5988792:x" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;shattered students' trust&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; in Cornell. Hundreds gathered Thursday night, some sobbing as they spoke. One student told Mann the woman at the center of the case "could have been any one of my friends or a classmate."&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tennessee tried to execute Christa Pike on Wednesday. She survived. &lt;/strong&gt;Pike, who was sentenced to death for the 1995 murder of Colleen Slemmer, remains in critical condition after receiving two doses of the lethal injection drug pentobarbital. Gov. Bill Lee has now &lt;a href="https://wpln.org/post/gov-lee-halts-execution-orders-third-party-review-following-pikes-failed-lethal-injection/" target="_blank"&gt;paused executions&lt;/a&gt; for the remainder of his term and ordered an independent review of what went wrong.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧&lt;strong&gt; It's the second failed execution in Tennessee this year.&lt;/strong&gt; WPLN's Marianna Bacallao says that one failed execution might be a fluke, but two suggest a pattern. Lee previously paused executions from 2022 to 2025 after a review found problems with the state's execution drugs. The current protocol &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5988792:x" target="_blank"&gt;grew out of that review&lt;/a&gt;, but the state is again investigating what went wrong.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The monthly jobs report will be released this morning. &lt;/strong&gt;For many Americans, the math is getting harder: prices are up, wages aren't keeping pace and borrowing costs more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;Forecasters expect today's report to show that employers added 80,000 to 90,000 jobs&lt;/strong&gt; in September, NPR's Scott Horsley says. That would be slower than August but stronger than earlier in the summer. Horsley says &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5988792:x" target="_blank"&gt;wage growth is another key measure&lt;/a&gt;, and pay increases aren't keeping pace with prices.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Renee Good's family &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/01/nx-s1-5986224/renee-good-ice-lawsuit-minneapolis" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;filed two civil lawsuits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; against the federal government yesterday &lt;/strong&gt;over her death last January. The 37-year-old was fatally shot by a federal agent during an immigration enforcement operation in Minnesota. The first lawsuit alleges ICE officer Jonathan Ross used excessive force. The second alleges that federal officials conspired to interfere with the civil rights of individuals in Minnesota.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's listen&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-145946" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 8256;         --source-height: 4644;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4644+0+430/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F16%2Fd4%2Fe63af9de44eb940a6f1320176c54%2Fgettyimages-2293950719.jpg" class="img" alt="Journalist and director Rachel Szor and Israeli journalist and filmmaker Yuval Abraham attend the photocall of &amp;quot;Naza&amp;quot; presented in competition at the 83rd International Venice Film Festival." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Journalist and director Rachel Szor and Israeli journalist and filmmaker Yuval Abraham attend the photocall of &lt;em&gt;Naza&lt;/em&gt; presented in competition at the 83rd International Venice Film Festival, at Venice Lido on Sept. 10, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Stefano Rellandini/AFP via Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;NAZA&lt;/em&gt; features 24 anonymous Israeli intelligence officers and soldiers describing the surveillance and targeting systems they used in Israel's war in Gaza – including AI — and the civilian deaths they say those systems allowed. Palestinian and international journalists have long documented that toll; the film brings testimony from inside the Israeli military system. Its title loosely translates to "collateral damage." The film turns that abstraction back into human lives. &lt;em&gt;NAZA&lt;/em&gt; opens in U.S. theaters this week after winning praise abroad, while in Israel it has drawn protests, accusations of treason and threats to revoke the filmmakers' citizenship.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;🎧 &lt;em&gt;Morning Edition&lt;/em&gt;'s Leila Fadel speaks with filmmakers Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor about what they learned and the &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5978797:x" target="_blank"&gt;backlash that followed&lt;/a&gt;. Listen to the &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5974309:x" target="_blank"&gt;full interview here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Weekend picks&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-145527" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5000;         --source-height: 2812;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5000x2812+0+159/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F13%2F6c%2F95a884574a5f85f7db0236b104b1%2Fgettyimages-2291214646.jpg" class="img" alt="Sheryl Crow performs in Nashville on Aug. 19, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Sheryl Crow performs in Nashville on Aug. 19, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Jason Kempin/Getty Images for ACM&lt;br&gt;                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Check out what &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/culture/" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NPR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt; is watching, reading and listening to this weekend:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🍿 Movies:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/29/nx-s1-5982735/forgotten-island-is-a-cluttered-feast-for-the-senses" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Forgotten Island&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; follows childhood friends Jo and Raissa, who are unexpectedly transported to a magical island just before they are about to part ways.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📺 TV:&lt;/strong&gt; The Spanish-language miniseries &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/01/nx-s1-5985845/my-sad-dead-review" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;My Sad Dead&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; follows an Argentinian doctor who can communicate with ghosts. &lt;em&gt;Fresh Air&lt;/em&gt; critic John Powers describes it as a unique blend of creepiness, sarcastic humor and political anger, unlike anything else on TV.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📚 Books:&lt;/strong&gt; Min Jin Lee's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/28/nx-s1-5982798/american-hagwon-min-jin-lee-review" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;American Hagwon&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the third installment in a planned four-novel series about the Korean diaspora. It explores the complexities of immigration, the fragile promise of America and the purpose of education.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎵 Music: &lt;/strong&gt;Now in her 60s, singer-songwriter Sheryl Crow says she has aged out of pop music. She describes her latest album, &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/01/nx-s1-5984965/sheryl-crow-pick-you-up" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pick You Up&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, as exploring questions many of us ask about our identity at this moment in humanity.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;❓ Quiz:&lt;/strong&gt; Bears, Beyoncé, and colleges. This week's news features a mix of serious headlines and lighter moments. Test your memory with &lt;a href="http://npr.org/2026/10/02/g-s1-145638/trump-hegseth-panda-ai-beyonce-news-quiz" target="_blank"&gt;this week's quiz&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-145890" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4153;         --source-height: 2336;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4153x2336+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fbe%2F12%2F29a56b2f41deabc5b8f65805d9f9%2Fgettyimages-2298077242.jpg" class="img" alt="A SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket and Dragon spacecraft carrying NASA&amp;#039;s Crew-13 lifts off Thursday from Cape Canaveral, Fla. SpaceX&amp;#039;s Crew Dragon capsule &amp;quot;Grace&amp;quot; will take NASA astronauts Jessica Watkins and Luke Delaney, Canadian Space Agency astronaut Joshua Kutryk, and Roscosmos cosmonaut Sergey Teteryatnikov to the International Space Station for about six months." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket and Dragon spacecraft carrying NASA's Crew-13 lifts off Thursday from Cape Canaveral, Fla. SpaceX's Crew Dragon capsule "Grace" will take NASA astronauts Jessica Watkins and Luke Delaney, Canadian Space Agency astronaut Joshua Kutryk, and Roscosmos cosmonaut Sergey Teteryatnikov to the International Space Station for about six months.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Justin Sullivan/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;SpaceX launched four astronauts on &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/01/nx-s1-5987698/nasa-crew-13-spacex-international-space-station-iss" target="_blank"&gt;NASA's Crew-13 mission&lt;/a&gt; to the International Space Station for a six-month stay before returning to Earth.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Google &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/01/nx-s1-5983697/project-suncatcher-google-ai-data-center-space" target="_blank"&gt;launched a refrigerator-sized satellite&lt;/a&gt; equipped with AI chips as part of Project Suncatcher, its effort to put AI data centers in space.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Pearly Kings were once a fixture of East London, raising money in their mother-of-pearl suits. Now, NPR &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/10/01/nx-s1-5928148/pearly-king-peckham-george-major-london-cockney" target="_blank"&gt;looks back at George Major&lt;/a&gt;, who died in August, and the tradition he helped carry on.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/1155154221/majd-al-waheidi"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Majd Al-Waheidi&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
