      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Good morning. You're reading the Up First newsletter. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/newsletter/news" target="_blank"&gt;Subscribe&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; here to get it delivered to your inbox, and &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/podcasts/510318/up-first/" target="_blank"&gt;listen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; to the Up First podcast for all the news you need to start your day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Today's top stories&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A flydubai plane headed to Tel Aviv yesterday made an emergency landing &lt;/strong&gt;after one pilot stabbed the other in a possible attempt to crash the plane. Most of the roughly 170 passengers were Israeli. Some passengers entered the cockpit and &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5985806/flydubai-flight-dubai-tel-aviv-israel" target="_blank"&gt;subdued the attacker&lt;/a&gt; after the injured pilot unlocked the door. Another flight crew on board then helped land the plane safely in Tabuk, Saudi Arabia. The motive remains unknown.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-145688" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2736;         --source-height: 1539;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2736x1539+0+142/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F5f%2F7fc0b4b24c3893ab85cb97f865b0%2Fgettyimages-2297341992.jpg" class="img" alt="A plane carrying passengers from an earlier flydubai flight that was diverted to Saudi Arabia arrives at Ben Gurion Airport on Wednesday in Tzafria, Israel. Earlier, their flight from the United Arab Emirates was diverted to Saudi Arabia after a violent altercation in the cockpit. A second plane was sent to Saudi Arabia to retrieve the stranded passengers and return them to Israel." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A plane carrying passengers from an earlier flydubai flight that was diverted to Saudi Arabia arrives at Ben Gurion Airport on Wednesday in Tzafria, Israel. Earlier, their flight from the United Arab Emirates was diverted to Saudi Arabia after a violent altercation in the cockpit. A second plane was sent to Saudi Arabia to retrieve the stranded passengers and return them to Israel.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Erik Marmor/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;NPR's Kat Lonsdorf was at the Tel Aviv airport as passengers returned.&lt;/strong&gt; She tells &lt;em&gt;Up First&lt;/em&gt; the arrivals area was packed with journalists and family members as passengers came through: some crying, some smiling and many looking exhausted. One passenger told Lonsdorf he tried to keep his young son calm during the ordeal. Another, a plumber, said he helped subdue the attacker and pulled up on the plane's controls after remembering something he had seen on TV. The incident comes less than a month before Israel's national election and is &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5986830:x" target="_blank"&gt;likely to become part of the campaign conversation&lt;/a&gt; in the weeks ahead.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;       &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;U.S. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth says he wants fewer generals and admirals &lt;/strong&gt;— and a military built around drones, AI and what he calls a "warrior ethos." In a speech at Quantico yesterday, Hegseth said he has already cut the number of senior officers by about 10% and &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5986304/hegseth-troops-address" target="_blank"&gt;wants to reach 20%&lt;/a&gt;. He also announced a new military command focused on drones and other emerging technologies, even as the U.S. remains at war with Iran.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧 &lt;strong&gt;NPR's Quil Lawrence says the issue is less about shrinking &lt;/strong&gt;the top ranks than about who Hegseth is removing and why. Hegseth has blocked some colonels from becoming generals without publicly explaining the decisions and has fired several senior officers. Lawrence also notes that the Pentagon has not held a news briefing since May, which is a &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5986830:x" target="_blank"&gt;stark contrast to the previous two decades&lt;/a&gt; of sometimes intense warfare in Iraq and Afghanistan.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The FBI says it is "aggressively" investigating a cyberattack &lt;/strong&gt;claimed by ShinyHunters after the group said it &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5985202/fbi-hack-shinyhunters" target="_blank"&gt;stole sensitive FBI employment data&lt;/a&gt;. It is still unclear how much information was taken or whether hackers got in through third-party software or the bureau's own systems. Some current and former employees told NPR the stolen files may include job applications, promotion records, family details and medical information.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;President Trump is traveling to Oklahoma today — &lt;/strong&gt;not a battleground state but a place where he can test-drive his midterm message with a friendly crowd. Trump promised to campaign for Republicans in 35 competitive races, but his first stops are in reliably red states like Oklahoma and Alabama.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🎧&lt;strong&gt; NPR's Franco Ordoñez says that the trips are partly about energizing voters&lt;/strong&gt; who reliably turn out for Trump but may be harder to motivate when he isn't on the ballot. Oklahoma also gives Trump a lower-risk &lt;a href="http://one.npr.org/i/nx-s1-5986830:x" target="_blank"&gt;place to try out campaign lines&lt;/a&gt; before heading to more competitive states, where his presence could just as easily motivate Democrats and independents.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Deep dive&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-144959" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 5280;         --source-height: 2970;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5280x2970+0+493/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F63%2F0a%2F41e0e8a0421882d549898cf146fc%2Fgettyimages-1434808195.jpg" class="img" alt="In an aerial view, the Strategic Petroleum Reserve storage at the Bryan Mound site is seen on October 19, 2022 in Freeport, Texas." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 In an aerial view, the Strategic Petroleum Reserve storage at the Bryan Mound site is seen on October 19, 2022 in Freeport, Texas.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Brandon Bell/Getty Images North America                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The U.S. has drawn heavily from its Strategic Petroleum Reserve since the war with Iran began, shrinking the stockpile by more than 30% in six months. The reserve, stored in underground salt caverns in Louisiana and Texas, is one of the government's main tools for easing pressure on gas prices. Here's &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/25/nx-s1-5965797/strategic-petroleum-reserve-low-level-venezuela" target="_blank"&gt;what to know&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;ul class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;🛢️ Rapid drawdowns can damage the reserve itself, putting stress on the salt caverns and other infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🛢️ The Trump administration is exploring a possible oil swap with Venezuela, though much of the crude under discussion is heavy and difficult to extract.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;🛢️ China has also tapped its reserves, but less aggressively as electric vehicles make up a larger share of transportation there.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Behind the story&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;by &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/279612138/geoff-brumfiel" target="_blank"&gt;&lt;u&gt;Geoff Brumfiel&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, NPR's senior editor and correspondent&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-144329" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 6200;         --source-height: 3488;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/6200x3488+0+581/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F35%2F6b%2F4d5113474763a720386f439bd345%2Fgettyimages-2294331667.jpg" class="img" alt="Tristan Buckmaster, mathematician at New York University, poses for a portrait in his office in Manhattan. He is wearing a white button down shirt and dark slacks. Behind him is a blackboard and a window. In front of him is a desk with a computer, keyboard and some papers." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Tristan Buckmaster is a mathematician at New York University. He poses for a portrait in his office in Manhattan on September 11, 2026. Buckmaster and his collaborator Levent Alpöge have been working on the Navier-Stokes equations. They are clashing with OpenAI, which claims to have cracked the equations.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Karsten Moran/for The Washington Post/Getty Images                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;OpenAI says its AI helped solve one of math's hardest problems. The catch? Mathematicians weren't quite sure how it got there.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;That's what I discovered when I started talking to mathematicians about what was supposed to be one of the biggest discoveries this century. It turned out OpenAI's GPT-6 Astra model was not some machine supergod that outstripped human intellect – it was just that it was really bad at showing its work.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;Suddenly, a very abstruse and vague math story felt pretty relatable. Who hasn't been scolded by a teacher for skipping the steps? And who hasn't gotten an AI answer that sounds impressive but leaves you wondering what on earth it just said?&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Mathematicians believe the answer is correct, but the AI-generated proof runs 166 pages, and they say it may take weeks to untangle what actually matters. Despite the lack of clarity, they're excited about the possibility of using AI to solve more problems in the future.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;You can read my &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/22/nx-s1-5968588/openai-navier-stokes-problem-mathematicians-learn-little" target="_blank"&gt;full reporting here&lt;/a&gt;. And if you come across an AI story you think I should be following, feel free to send it my way via Signal at gbrumfiel.13.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;3 things to know before you go&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-145643" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2000;         --source-height: 1125;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1125+0+152/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fd7%2F06%2F92fb3d454823b47041801337f49b%2F03-clariden-mhuss.jpg" class="img" alt="A Swiss glacier shows the effects of years of ice loss, with exposed rock replacing ice that once covered the landscape." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A Swiss glacier shows the effects of years of ice loss, with exposed rock replacing ice that once covered the landscape.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Swiss Academy of Natural Sciences                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;ol class="edTag"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Switzerland's glaciers &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5981403/swiss-glaciers-climate-change" target="_blank"&gt;lost more than 5% of their ice&lt;/a&gt; in 2026, another stark year in a long-running decline driven by global warming.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A year after the $7,500 federal EV tax credit disappeared, here's how electric and hybrid vehicles &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5979915/ev-hybrid-sales-2026-federal-tax-credit" target="_blank"&gt;have fared in the market&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Postcard from Damascus: NPR's Emily Feng &lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/2026/09/30/nx-s1-5983516/damascus-syria-glass" target="_blank"&gt;visits a glassmaker&lt;/a&gt; working through Syria's punishing summer heat.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;   &lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This newsletter was edited by &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/1155154221/majd-al-waheidi"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Majd Al-Waheidi&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.npr.org/people/859721331/suzanne-nuyen"target="_blank"   &gt;&lt;em&gt;Suzanne Nuyen&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; contributed.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
